ntnhcore.questtext.9f6f4fa8eca2838baf3ae:
#{ffce86}The legacy event is absent#{reset}
NTNH 1.7.10's RandomThings is not installed in Second Dawn. Its Blood Moon is not verified here and is not recommended as a way to obtain launch codes or a Geiger counter.

Hostile creatures from installed mods remain part of survival, but their presence should not be described as the old RandomThings event. Prepare protection and check current acquisition methods.

ntnhcore.questtext.b539f7db723c34c2ae8d9:
The #{00aaaa}CO2 Scrubber#{reset} is a mechanism for cleaning air in sealed environments under increased pressure.

The device absorbs #{55ffff}Carbon Dioxide#{reset} from the surrounding air and collects it. It only works if two conditions are met: the room is sealed and isolated, and the air pressure is elevated (above 1.0 atm). The latter can be achieved by adding a stream of #{55ffff}Oxygen#{reset} from the ventilation to the Earth's air (resulting in a total pressure of 1.1 atm).

#{00aa00}The maximum number of scrubbers in a room is 5; any additional units placed will not collect carbon dioxide.#{reset}

ntnhcore.questtext.fdc3ae19cb0e6c578feeb:
Jool is a gas giant planet with Laythe and two other small unnamed planets orbiting it.

As is logical, landing on a gas giant is impossible, but this doesn't prevent us from gathering resources from this giant.

#{00aa00}Jool's atmosphere consists of #{55ffff}Helium-3#{reset} #{00aa00}(25%), #{55ffff}Liquid Hydrogen#{reset} #{00aa00}(25%), #{55ffff}Chlorine#{reset} #{00aa00}(20%), and #{55ffff}Neon#{reset} #{00aa00}(12%). To collect all these gases, we will need a #{00aaaa}Harvester#{reset}.#{reset}

ntnhcore.questtext.329410dcd16488ffc7649:
