ntnhcore.questtext.c5e0321c54ee31ffd3d8d:
#{ffce86}A direction for progression#{reset}
Second Dawn includes NTM Continuum Space. Space remains part of the pack's development direction, but that is not a promise of a complete start-to-finish run on every planet.

The original NTNH Martian mode is not verified as a finished Second Dawn scenario. Planetary generation, resources and supply chains need further testing. Follow available milestones and prepare protection, supplies and a return route before travel. See Known Issues.

ntnhcore.questtext.0560c7ca5d864c090beed:
#{ffce86}Food modules#{reset}
Four Pam’s HarvestCraft 2 modules are installed: Food Core, Food Extended, Crops and Trees. They provide ingredients, crops, trees and meals. Modern content differs from HarvestCraft 1.7.10; old fish, bee, market and shipping-bin claims are not instructions for this pack.

#{ffce86}AgriCraft#{reset}
AgriCraft uses crop sticks, plant traits and crossbreeding. Soil, light and other requirements depend on the crop. Do not assume every Pam’s crop supports every planting method; check the crops and recipes present in this version.

#{ffce86}Getting started#{reset}
Begin with available seeds and a small farm with water and light. Check seed acquisition and recipes in JEI. Hunger Overhauled changes hoe use, harvesting and growth rates; legacy 1.7.10 tables may differ from current settings.

ntnhcore.questtext.667715cb71f6a4758bfcf:
#{ffce86}Hunger is part of survival#{reset}
Hunger Overhauled is installed. The current common config enables constant hunger loss and low hunger/health effects; starvation damage is set very high. Do not let your food supply run out.

Food values, stack size and eating speed are modified by configuration. Well Fed is enabled and assists healing. Check actual food properties in game and recipes in JEI.

#{ffce86}Variety and health#{reset}
Spice of Life: Carrot Edition tracks distinct foods eaten and grants extra hearts at configured milestones. A new food does not necessarily grant a heart immediately; repeating the same food does not increase variety.

#{ffce86}Growing food#{reset}
Growth is slowed in configuration, with an additional delay without sunlight rather than a complete ban. Removal of wooden/stone hoe recipes and modified hoe use are enabled. Check individual AgriCraft crop requirements separately. Establish a reliable food supply before broadening your menu.

