ntnhcore.quest.14081.desc:
#{ffce86}Quest migration#{reset}
47 pending legacy objectives occur in 27 quests. These quests cannot be completed normally until their required objectives are implemented; dependent milestones may also stay locked. This is not the number of all locked quests for an individual player.

#{ffce86}Unavailable systems#{reset}
OpenComputers, Computronics and OpenSecurity are absent and their port is postponed. CC:Tweaked is installed but is not a compatible replacement for legacy computers or programs. Classic GuideNH construction animations are not ported. Some legacy rewards, recipes and optional components are still missing.

#{ffce86}Observed errors#{reset}
Testing reproduced a WorldEdit conversion exception during server startup and OpenGL depth-format mismatch messages. The client and server started, but this does not establish compatibility with every GPU. Full planetary generation, reactor and progression testing is incomplete.

#{ffce86}Saves and bug reports#{reset}
Do not delete the world or quest progress to troubleshoot. Before updating, back up the complete world together with mods and configs. Include the pack version, Java, reproduction steps and a redacted log in reports. Project contact addresses may not yet be published; do not send Second Dawn issues to NTNH's old support channel.

ntnhcore.quest.15361.desc:
#{ffce86}Technology-focused survival#{reset}
Second Dawn rewards learning complex systems gradually. Keep food and tools ready, monitor radiation and do not test an unfamiliar reactor beside your main base.

Difficulty does not excuse a broken recipe or incorrect advice. For an objective that does not register, first check the item, amount and quest availability, then keep details for a bug report. Deleting progress is not a troubleshooting step.

ntnhcore.quest.15617.desc:
#{ffce86}Installed interface mods#{reset}
Jade supplies block/entity information. Xaero’s Minimap and World Map provide maps; check their menus and control bindings for display settings.

The original pack's In-Game Info is not installed. /igi config, /igi enable and /igi disable are not presented as working commands here.

#{ffce86}Graphics#{reset}
Embeddium is installed. Start with Minecraft's video settings: render distance, FPS limit and VSync. Change one setting at a time and compare results. Oculus and OptiFine are not included; third-party shader support is unverified. The legacy Fancy Textures advice does not apply.

For rendering errors, keep the log and GPU details. Scrolling JEI is not a verified fix.

ntnhcore.quest.21761.desc:
#{ffce86}From tools to a stable base#{reset}
Start with available flint tools, food, light and shelter. Early quests introduce survival changes and preparation for industry. Check actual recipes in JEI.

Complete required objectives in available quests; optional ones remain optional. Distinguish normal prerequisites from unsupported port objectives. A safe base and spare supplies help you move into materials processing.

ntnhcore.quest.23041.desc:
#{ffce86}Keep building#{reset}
You have explored Second Dawn's opening stage. Expand materials processing and production before moving toward more complex power and automation.

Check recipes in JEI and leave room for safe expansion. A full playthrough of the adaptation is not yet verified; consult Known Issues if you encounter an unsupported objective, keeping your current progress intact.

ntnhcore.quest.24833.desc:
#{ffce86}Quests and recipes#{reset}
The book guides progression and explains major steps. JEI shows actually registered recipes; check them before crafting. Individual mods may provide their own manuals when the corresponding book or interface exists in game.

#{ffce86}Changes since 1.7.10#{reset}
The classic GuideNH book and its miniature construction animations are not ported. There is no working GuideNH opening key to recommend. Installing Patchouli and GuideME does not by itself restore legacy pages or animations.

Legacy NTNH references may describe another HBM version. For discrepancies, consult current recipes and Known Issues, then report through Second Dawn's contacts once available.

ntnhcore.quest.25089.desc:
#{ffce86}A second dawn starts small#{reset}
Nuclear Tech: Second Dawn is an independent pack about survival, rebuilding industry and using nuclear technology responsibly. Begin with flint tools and a safe base, then progress through materials, automation, HBM power and space exploration.

#{ffce86}The core experience#{reset}
HBM NTM Continuum and Space form the technological foundation. Radiation, hazardous materials, pollution and hostile creatures reward preparation. JEI shows actual recipes; Applied Energistics 2 supports storage and later automation. A varied food supply, farms and protective equipment matter alongside new machinery.

#{ffce86}Your first steps#{reset}
Read the quest and food guidance, make flint tools and prepare a base. Follow available quests; optional objectives are not required. Learn unfamiliar machines in a small, safe setup first.

#{ffce86}Where this book comes from#{reset}
The quest structure is adapted from Nuclear Tech: New Horizons for Minecraft 1.7.10. This is not an entirely original Second Dawn book or an official NTNH release. The original work by SkippyPlaysMC for NTI/STI, Bufka2011's revision and contributions from the NTNH community are acknowledged in Credits.

#{ffce86}Development status#{reset}
The adaptation is still in development. Some legacy objectives remain unavailable; a complete playthrough of every branch and planet has not been verified. Back up your world before updating. See Known Issues. GitHub Issues and Discord buttons become available once genuine project addresses are configured.

ntnhcore.quest.25345.desc:
#{ffce86}Progression map#{reset}
Large icons mark major milestones. Side quests sit below their corresponding main quests; arrows show prerequisites. An ordinary future quest lock differs from a pending-port message: the latter means an objective is missing from this adaptation.

#{ffce86}Objectives and rewards#{reset}
Available inventory collection objectives are checked automatically. Detect/Submit remains available for manual checks and exchanges. Submission objectives may consume items, so read the objective first. Optional objectives are not required. Claim rewards separately; a claimed non-repeatable reward cannot be claimed again.

#{ffce86}Playing together#{reset}
The party button opens Better Questing's own party system. FTB Teams and FTB Chunks are separate; joining an FTB team does not automatically create a quest party. Shared rewards are not guaranteed for every reward type. Test invitations, shared progress and claiming with a simple quest before a group playthrough.

ServerUtilities is not installed. FTB Chunks handles claims; limits and forced chunk loading depend on server settings and player permissions. Unattended reactors in unloaded areas have not been verified.

#{ffce86}Controls#{reset}
Open the book with `, the physical key below Esc; its label depends on keyboard layout. Q remains the drop-item key. See Controls to customize bindings. Back returns to the previous screen; long descriptions and objectives scroll separately.

This book is based on work by SkippyPlaysMC, Bufka2011 and the NTNH community. See Credits for attribution.

